@page rh="THE FALL · V · FOUNDER FILES · THE LEDGER AND THE DISSENT" m="TKC: TL · FR 40–44"
# The ledger and the Covenant of Dissent
rec:
2098 | During a Crown advisory access period, Azrael found a ledger in the east wing archive. It ties the Empire's founding documents to a series of deliberate removals, which the Covenant of Purpose describes as God's order and the ledger describes as something else. It had sat there unmoved since 2085, because nobody was looking (FR 41).
Put it back | He took it to his father, who told him to put it back. Azrael kept it and went looking for its companion, the Covenant of Dissent, which Elias wrote in the same year and the same hand, as the theological counter-argument to everything the Empire was built on.
2100 | Dorian removed both documents the week Azrael was declared dead (FR 42). He'd told Azrael to put the ledger back because a document Azrael had read and returned would be one Dorian controlled. Destroying it would have told Azrael it mattered (FR 43).
plate: doc
dh: East Wing Archive · Holdings Card | CATALOGUED UNTIL 2100
df: Item | Covenant of Dissent, in the hand of E. Vane
df: Companion item | Ledger, uncatalogued
df: Last withdrawn | ________________________________
df: Status | missing, the week of 2100 in which A. Vane was declared dead
stamp: WITHDRAWN
/end
prompt: What the "deliberate removals" were: people, populations, records, or all three | fill

